    "description": "``sqrt()`` is a PHP native function, that computes the square root of a number. That function takes a integer or a float, and returns the same types, depending on the actual value of the result.\n\n``sqrt()`` is not a particularly slow function. The opposite of ``sqrt()`` is ``** 2``, or ``pow($x, 2)``, or even ``$x * $x``, where ``$x`` is the result of ``sqrt()``.",
